  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Gates",
      "items": [
        "Verifier gates are prepared bound at delegation from author_keys; the verifier needs the verify grant and cannot verify its own work",
        "A verdict binds to one revision and delta hash; any new write clears it",
        "Shell staging: shell-prepare projects the scope, shell-complete stages the captured result"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Consolidation",
      "items": [
        "Orchestrator-only; a verdict is required only for maintenance cycles",
        "Flush writes a manifest, replaces files one by one, then verifies bases",
        "A maintenance cycle's flush is retained until the cycle completes; until then the cycle can be discarded"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Recovery",
      "items": [
        "While recovery is pending every call is refused",
        "Invoking the original normal operation as the orchestrator asks for exact-state approval: it restores the pre-flush snapshot, or keeps divergent current files and closes the effect as interrupted with evidence, then reevaluates the original operation",
        "Repair approval never authorizes consolidation; ownership, current verdicts and physical bases are checked again",
        "A restore refuses when a base changed; divergent files are kept and closed interrupted rather than overwritten"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Claims and reads",
      "items": [
        "claim_assign without an author_key never takes a path another root's claim holds; continue that work with its author_key, or release or discard it first",
        "claim_assign with the work's author_key keeps its staged work; naming only part of it hands that part over under a new key",
        "A declared reads selector lifts claims of work no one runs and serves its staged view; it is refused while covered work is in flight, and so is a claim over what an in-flight unit reads",
        "Liveness requires a prelaunch binding or the binding's own active attempt; another attempt of the same unit does not keep it live",
        "Reassign keeps the staged delta and clears the verdict; revoke frees paths and is refused while work is staged",
        "vfs_discard is orchestrator-only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ordinary shell network",
      "items": [
        "TAKT_SANDBOX_ALLOWED_DOMAINS carries comma-separated domain patterns; when supplied, the ordinary shell wrapper initializes a strict proxy allowlist",
        "Unset or empty leaves the network unrestricted; the adapter API's explicit [] denies domains, but the environment parser returns nil for empty input",
        "This is not a default deny-all policy; D05 and D06 remain uncertified"
      ]
    }
  ]
